WEBVTT

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:32.860
Former I-1 Mayushi's Sendai idol WUG thread 
Entertainment Production Company "Green Leaves Entertainment" HP 

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.200
Former I-1's Mayushi is back!! 
Sendai TV's concert was awesome! 
I'm glad I followed her...

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.200
Why?

00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:41.800
You sure she's not just struggling in vain? 

00:01:41.850 --> 00:01:43.700
Isn't Mayu that piece of trash who betrayed her fans with a man?

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.750
She's a problem girl 
so terrible Shiraki 
chased her 
out lololol

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:48.230
It's just the opposite. 
She was touched by lolicon Shiraki and thrown away. So sad lol

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.250
I'm impressed she made such a brazen return

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:50.710
Unbelievable. 
Don't underestimate the countryside!

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:55.630
Why is everyone taking it so badly?

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.220
In the end, isn't this a good thing?

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:07.230
"In the end, isn't this a good thing?"

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:07.390
In the end, isn't this a good thing...

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:09.100
Are you stupid?

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:10.560
What's good? Explain

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.610
The real tragedy 
is that the other members 
are being forced along with this trash

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.230
They're old news. 
Poor WUG lololol

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:17.320
What is this?

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:19.250
Mayushi?

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:20.320
Shimada Mayu, huh?

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:25.330
Yes. She's working with 
Sendai's Wake Up, Girls!

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.870
The rumors were true.

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.710
<b>Internal Conflict in I-1?</b>

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.710
<b>Shimada Mayu retires?!</b>

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.710
<b>Shimada Mayu leaves?!</b>

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.710
Our next project has been decided.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.390
You're going to cover Mayushi?

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.970
Yeah.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:42.470
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.850
Yes, yes.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.470
Thank you.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:51.600
Boss?

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:53.790
Um...

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.360
<b>Airi</b>

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.360
Like this?

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:58.360
No, no. A signature 
should look like this.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:02:59.500
No way.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.270
What? You think so?

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:04.080
Hey, isn't this cute?

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.140
Is that a paper doll?

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.620
No.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:13.180
Airi, where's Mayushi?

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.330
I haven't heard.

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.780
I wonder what's going on with her.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.380
She's not usually late.

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:21.880
Listen up, girls.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.400
I found your next job.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.140
Dance with joy.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.480
After your TV performance,

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.690
you're going to be 
regulars on a radio show.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:32.900
What?!

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:34.700
You're going to be regulars 
on a daily program.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.450
On top of that, it's a title show.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.710
It's a one-minute segment 
from 11:59 pm to midnight.

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:40.530
So short.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.090
Daily and title?

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:46.530
Um...

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:48.970
Daily means it's every day.

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.350
Title means our name 
appears in the title of the show.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:54.790
That's amazing.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.280
No, no, no.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:58.570
This is a small step.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.970
We're aiming for the Red vs. White Concert.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.170
A journey of a thousand 
miles starts with one step.

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.790
By the way, how many 
miles away is the

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:05.800
Red vs. White Concert Hall from here?

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.240
I don't know.

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.900
We definitely have good 
things coming our way.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.240
We'll fearlessly move forward.

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:13.310
Yes!

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.670
You know what they say.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.780
The god of chance only has bangs.

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.010
Honestly, what does that mean?

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.700
Good morning.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.700
Anna, Karina.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.040
It's been a while, everyone.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.450
Good morning.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:33.710
You seem excited.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.380
We are. Let me tell you all about it.

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:50.220
Why is she doing this again?

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:53.230
If she wanted to do it, 
she never should have given up!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:55.620
If you say that, there's no hope.

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:58.760
You should consider 
how Mayu-chan feels.

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.780
Isn't this the result of 
respecting her thoughts?

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.010
I'm leaving now.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:14.750
<b>New Song</b>

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:14.060
In any case, I'm having Twinkle 
write a second original song for us.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:22.760
<b>New Song</b>

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:17.160
The condition for the first song

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.580
was that it be one total amateurs could

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.760
look good singing and dancing...

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.260
You've gone too far.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.760
But we need another one like that.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:28.230
What does that mean?

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:31.320
Does that mean we haven't grown?

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:32.620
That's exactly right.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.020
Sorry I'm late.

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.400
I-I'm sorry!

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:41.440
Don't worry about it.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.600
We just suddenly dropped in.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.620
Anyway, this is how long a minute is.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:52.720
What are we supposed to do in that time?

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.620
Really? I think it's pretty long.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:58.730
But if we divide 60 seconds 
among seven people,

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:00.090
each person gets just over eight seconds.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:01.630
How long is that?

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.640
Let's give it a try.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:04.450
Good evening.

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:07.400
It's time for the Wake Up, Girls! 
"Sorry It's So Short!" program.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.410
I'm Nanase Yoshino.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.460
Is it too conventional to say my hobbies

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.390
are reading and watching films?

00:06:13.230 --> 00:06:14.750
That's it, I guess.

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.270
I'm Miyu. Hello.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:21.540
What's everyone's 
favorite type of omu-rice?

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:23.310
Omu-rice is omu-rice.

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:25.650
I'm talking about the 
words you write on top.

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.270
Oh! It's over.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:29.060
Kayatan, you interrupted me.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.570
I'm next.

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:31.940
I'm Kikuma Kaya.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:35.140
Looking at the sea 
makes me feel kind of sad.

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.410
So gloomy.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.530
Ready, go!

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:41.170
<b>New Song</b>

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.120
I love cream yakisoba bread.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.100
People ask me if I ever get 
sick of it, but I never do.

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.800
You didn't say your name, Minami.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:45.420
Huh?

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:49.960
Uh, um...

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:51.440
Japanese sweets...

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:52.150
It's over.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:53.130
You're kidding!

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.730
I didn't get to say anything, Mayushi.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.290
Mayushi?

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.180
Oh, sorry.

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.090
Is something wrong?

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:02.440
Are you not feeling well?

00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:04.980
No, nothing like that.

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.210
Is there anything we can say that will

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:09.950
express our individuality in a word?

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.200
Oh! What about weird faces?

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:14.700
But it's radio.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:17.700
You're right.

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.260
That should do it.

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:27.890
I made a lot of requests for this song,

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:31.070
but I basically trust your musical sense.

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:34.720
If anything, you should forget 
what the president said.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.020
That girl who was late...

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:38.860
Oh, Shimada Mayu?

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:40.730
She's a member now.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:44.230
Yes, she joined partway through.

00:07:44.570 --> 00:07:46.060
Please let me be an idol!

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:51.570
She'd been turning us down,
 but ultimately, she came to us.

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:54.820
She quit once, and now she's starting again.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:59.580
There's something cloudy 
about the color of her aura, though.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:03.830
When she quit the I-1 Club, 
it was pretty sensational.

00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:09.350
She may have a lot weighing on her.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.290
The god of chance, huh?

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:16.000
Everyone does experience 
good luck at least once.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.830
They say what's important is whether

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:19.850
or not you grab that opportunity.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:24.160
Work, lambs!

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.870
First, a TV show, and now a radio program.

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:30.350
The pressure's building.

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:32.290
Mayushi, what do you think?

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:35.920
Did you ever get nervous 
when you were part of the I-1 Club?

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.620
Well, yes...

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:45.500
Um... The reason you quit the I-1 Club...

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:48.750
I'm sorry.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:53.020
I was a little tired then.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.900
Maybe I shouldn't have come back.

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:03.800
What?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:08.570
A Izumi Chuo train 
is arriving at Platform Two.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:12.910
For your safety, please stand 
behind the white line.

00:09:14.090 --> 00:09:16.340
Never mind. It's nothing.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.210
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.210
What? You want to pick us up 
for a documentary program?

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:27.040
Is this on a national network?

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.990
Yes. We heard Wake Up, Girls!

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:36.090
has been working hard in Sendai, 
and we'd like to cover you.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:37.680
What do you think?

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:43.230
You must be sharp to set 
your sights on us, TTX.

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:44.960
Thank you.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:46.490
Did she go for it?

00:09:48.230 --> 00:09:51.170
I'll e-mail you the details.

00:09:51.170 --> 00:09:52.490
Could I have your address?

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:53.690
Okay.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:56.190
<b>I-1 Shimada Mayu leaves?</b>

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:00.880
President?

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:02.580
Yes!

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.580
Tokyo's finally moving!

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:05.450
What?

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.900
With former I-1 member 
Mayu in our group,

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:11.360
I expected this to happen 
sooner or later...

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:13.960
but this is sooner than I expected.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.430
The title of the program is

00:10:15.430 --> 00:10:19.470
<i>On the Brink of Their Break! 
Country Idols to Keep Your Eye On!</i>

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:22.150
A Tokyo TV station?

00:10:22.150 --> 00:10:23.160
Really?

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:24.230
Huh...

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:25.750
Is it on a national network?

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:26.990
That's amazing.

00:10:26.990 --> 00:10:29.230
But why us?

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.780
Because you're shining.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:33.980
You know... like a diamond in the rough.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:36.490
Does that mean we've been found?

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:39.250
I suppose that's what it means.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:40.570
Amazing...

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:41.780
This is really amazing.

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.860
Wow!

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.560
This is so amazing!

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.730
Hello.

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:18.370
Good work on your lessons.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:20.230
You seem to be working hard.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:22.540
All you can do is work hard.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.930
We don't need girls who can't work hard.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:28.020
I hope you'll keep working hard.

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.100
Yes, sir!

00:11:30.040 --> 00:11:35.430
With the "I-1 Club National 47 
Prefecture Love Connection Project"

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:37.800
progressing well,

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:43.630
the Sendai Theater's opening 
concert will be held next month.

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:46.180
The participating members will be 
the names I announced yesterday.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:47.500
Yes, sir!

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.690
The I-1 members going 
to Sendai are the very best.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:58.250
I hope the I-2 and I-3 members 
who will cover them in the event

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:03.660
anything should occur 
are doing their very best, as well.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:04.520
Yes, sir!

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:07.060
Now, quickly shifting gears,

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.200
I'd like to announce this month's rejects.

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:17.210
134, 170, 209, 511.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.320
Good-bye, the four of you.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:21.110
Starting tomorrow, 
you don't need to come.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:23.970
I will now announce 
their new replacements.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:31.480
Ten girls numbered 1120 through 
1129 are joining the I-1 Club today.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:37.760
Let us conclude this day 
by singing the necessary attributes

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:39.090
of a popular idol together.

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:40.080
Yes, sir!

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:43.780
Don't rest! Don't complain! Don't think!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:46.490
Don't rest! Don't complain! Don't think!

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:48.360
Gratitude, always!

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.740
Gratitude, always!

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:52.750
Sendai's next month.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:54.580
Sendai, huh?

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.590
Last month was Nara. 
The month before that was Niigata.

00:12:57.590 --> 00:12:59.380
We're traveling all across Japan.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.510
Anyway... Do you know about this?

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.130
What?

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.380
You're kidding! Mayu?

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.890
It's her.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:12.170
I can't believe she's working in Sendai.

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:13.990
I'm kind of surprised.

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:16.390
It seemed like she 
would never work again.

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.890
Why is she coming back now?

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:20.460
She gave up on being an idol.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:23.650
Why would she bother working 
in the countryside, anyway?

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:25.950
Isn't it obvious?

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:28.160
Because she loves it.

00:13:28.590 --> 00:13:32.410
But we're going to go 
crush her next month.

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:59.940
<b>From: Yoshikawa Megumi 
Subject: It's been a while!</b>

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:51.910
<i>It's been a while!</i>

00:13:51.910 --> 00:13:55.020
<i>I saw a Wake Up, Girls! video today.</i>

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:58.090
<i>You've starting working again in Sendai.</i>

00:13:58.090 --> 00:13:59.940
<i>You should have told me.</i>

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:05.230
<i>I'm glad you returned 
to this business, though.</i>

00:14:05.230 --> 00:14:08.040
<i>I hope we can stand 
on the same stage together.</i>

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:11.950
<i>I'll be on the I-1 Sendai stage next month.</i>

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.930
<i>Come see us.</i>

00:14:16.280 --> 00:14:18.390
I'm going to talk to the president!

00:14:18.390 --> 00:14:19.910
It's no use.

00:14:19.910 --> 00:14:22.210
But this...

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:24.710
This isn't fair!

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:26.910
Don't cry, Mayu.

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:32.820
<i>It's been a while.</i>

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:34.920
<i>Sorry about Wake Up, Girls!</i>

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:36.470
<i>I didn't mean to keep it a secret.</i>

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:41.230
<i>I meant to tell you 
when I had set things right.</i>

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:45.570
<i>I want to stand on the 
same stage with you, too.</i>

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:47.790
<i>Good luck with your performance in Sendai.</i>

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.740
You can do it,

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:50.740
Mayu!

00:14:55.740 --> 00:15:04.000
<b>Green Leaves Entertainment</b>

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:59.390
I'm Green Leaves' 
representative, Tange Junko.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:02.520
This blockhead is 
our manager, Matsuda.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.000
I'm Matsuda Kohei.

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:05.620
I'm Suzuki.

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:07.880
Thank you for meeting us today.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.240
I'm his assistant, Yamada.

00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:11.260
It's nice to meet you.

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:13.360
The pleasure is ours.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:17.170
We've spoken with 
representatives of our regular TV

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:20.020
and radio programs, 
and they've approved an interview.

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.170
I see.

00:15:22.170 --> 00:15:23.980
How long will this take?

00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.420
Let's get to it, then.

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:29.900
I was hoping to talk to the members.

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:32.620
I see.

00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.160
Let's get started.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:38.890
I'd like to ask each member 
some simple questions in turn

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:40.660
and have them answer.

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:42.420
Start rolling whenever.

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:45.780
Let's start with your reason for joining.

00:15:45.780 --> 00:15:47.990
Nanase-san, you're first.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:48.680
Okay.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:53.270
Why did you become an idol?

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.780
I'm Nanase Yoshino.

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:58.450
I'm originally from Sendai,

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:01.350
and I've been a child talent star 
since I was four years old.

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:04.060
At one point, I wanted to be a model,

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.690
but I decided to pursue 
a career as an idol.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.230
I see. Thank you.

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:11.190
Next, Kikuma Kaya-san.

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:12.280
Okay.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.490
Same question.

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:19.760
I'm Kikuma Kaya.

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:22.170
I'd been working a lot of jobs,

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:25.480
and I found out about 
this audition at one of them.

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:30.090
I wanted some proof of my 
accomplishments, so I decided to try out.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:31.750
I see.

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:32.880
Next person, please.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:40.670
Um... Shimada Mayu-san.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:42.140
Yes.

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:48.360
I'm Shimada Mayu.

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:53.580
You're former I-1 Club member, 
Mayushi, aren't you?

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:54.280
Yes.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.100
Sorry to be direct,

00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:58.840
but the real reason you were 
made to quit the I-1 Club

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:02.620
was different from what 
the media covered, isn't it?

00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:08.710
The official story is that 
you lost a center battle,

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:10.990
but according to my research,

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:13.910
you were involved in a lot 
of internal conflicts.

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.010
What happened?

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:19.530
Come on! You quit.

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:22.020
Why don't you tell the truth?

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:23.520
Hey!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:33.780
Was the reason this picture 
that everyone was talking about?

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:39.370
There are rumors of power 
struggles within the group

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:42.990
and suspiciously large money 
transfers, aren't there?

00:17:43.780 --> 00:17:45.810
What's Shiraki-san like?

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:48.760
Did something happen 
between you and Shiraki-san?

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:53.050
Oh? Am I right?

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:54.420
Whoa!

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:57.680
That's enough!

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:03.430
Wasn't the purpose of today's 
interview to cover Wake Up, Girls!?

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:05.680
Shimada Mayu's history
 has nothing to do with this.

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:09.290
You must be confused.

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:14.190
Wake Up, Girls! doesn't exist 
without Shimada Mayu, does it?

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:17.520
Isn't it better for you

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:22.700
if people make a fuss over 
Shimada Mayu on the internet?

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:22.700
"The Struggles of the Fallen Idol"

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.750
That's enough!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:30.710
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:28.400
I'll sue!

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.710
Go ahead and try!

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:42.020
Today was rough.

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:43.230
Where's Mayu?

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:45.720
The president wanted to talk to her.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:46.620
But...

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:49.450
Let's leave it up to the president today.

00:18:49.450 --> 00:18:51.230
You've got work tomorrow.

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:53.480
Okay...

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:09.560
I'm not sure I can say 
anything to cheer you up now.

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:14.110
Without having experienced 
what you've gone through,

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:16.500
nothing I say is very convincing.

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:20.490
But let me tell you this.

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.470
Everyone has emotional scars.

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:27.580
However, you can't leave 
those wounds untreated.

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:32.250
I'm sure you know how 
to heal those wounds.

00:19:33.050 --> 00:19:34.770
Isn't that why you came here?

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:50.540
I wonder if Mayushi's okay.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.370
We don't exist without 
Shimada Mayu, huh?

00:19:53.890 --> 00:19:55.040
He was pretty harsh, wasn't he?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:58.400
If we don't want people 
to think that way,

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:02.120
we have to improve our skills 
to be on par with Mayushi's.

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.050
Anyway...

00:20:03.780 --> 00:20:05.300
The reason Mayu quit I-1?

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:10.230
Yeah. I know people were 
making quite a fuss,

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:12.850
but something seems pretty 
malicious about it.

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:15.310
Have you heard anything, Ai-chan?

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:19.690
I try not to ask her about it.

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:22.570
It seems like Mayu 
doesn't want me to ask.

00:20:23.750 --> 00:20:24.680
I understand.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:27.210
Who cares about the past?

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:29.830
It doesn't seem to be over yet.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:31.580
What do you mean?

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:38.710
I wonder if Mayushi saw this.

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:39.990
It's so mean.

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:43.840
She probably ended up seeing this.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:44.970
Isn't Mayu that piece of trash who 
betrayed her fans with a man?

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:46.550
Is this true?

00:20:47.000 --> 00:20:51.160
According to the customers 
at the maid café, they're mostly lies,

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:53.840
but there are some 
they can't be sure of.

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:56.560
Does that mean only 
Mayu knows the truth?

00:20:56.560 --> 00:21:01.390
Actually, I tried asking 
Mayushi directly before,

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:03.950
but she wouldn't tell me.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:05.930
She should talk to someone about it,

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:07.620
instead of handling it on her own.

00:21:07.940 --> 00:21:10.010
Maybe she can't do that right now.

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:13.000
Are you saying she doesn't trust us?

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:14.620
That's not what I meant.

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:16.870
Maybe it's not easy for her to say.

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:19.630
That just means she's not 
ready to talk about it.

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:24.650
Is this what it's like to live 
in the entertainment industry?

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:30.850
Get out! 
Comeback idol

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:31.850
What is she 
trying to do now?

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:32.640
Is she trying to get back at I-1 
for firing her? Seriously crazy

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:41.840
<i>Taking back a dream you've lost</i>

00:21:41.840 --> 00:21:46.060
<i>must be harder than 
achieving it the first time.</i>

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:53.190
<i>That's why I want to support 
Shimada Mayu's desire to try again.</i>

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:09.550
Shiho?

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:11.970
Mayu?

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:14.970
To be continued

00:23:44.980 --> 00:23:48.000
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:45.450 --> 00:23:47.890
Mayushi's a very mysterious girl.

00:23:47.890 --> 00:23:48.660
Yeah.

00:23:48.660 --> 00:23:51.380
Ai-chan, you're her friend. 
You must know a lot about her.

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:52.420
Not at all.

00:23:52.420 --> 00:23:54.240
Oh, but I do know one thing.

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:54.740
What?

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:56.130
The number of moles on her body.

00:23:56.130 --> 00:23:57.360
What a maniac.

00:23:57.360 --> 00:24:00.250
The next episode is 
"Heaven or Hell!"

00:23:57.470 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"Heaven or Hell"</b>
